node.doctext:
Hi,

<p>I have the same symptoms as above.</p>
<p>I have a full-fledged service based on Win32::Daemon.</p>
<p>It is working correctly on at least 5 computers.</p>
<p>On the remaining computers, the section in the if statement shown below never executes.</p>
<p>I have modeled after example 5 on https://metacpan.org/pod/Win32%3A%3ADaemon</p>
<code>
sub Callback_Running {
	my($Event, $Context) = @_;
print "State: " . Win32::Daemon::State() . "\n";
	if(SERVICE_RUNNING == Win32::Daemon::State()) {
		Log 1, "DBSAgent is checking in.";;	
</code>
<p>On the server I can troubleshoot on, State displayed as 1: SERVICE_STOPPED on the first call, then 0: SERVICE_NOT_READY on each call after that.  It never displayed as 4: SERVICE_RUNNING like it was supposed to.</p>
<p>The server I am troubleshooting on is Windows Server 2012 R2 Standard 64-bit v6.3.9600</p>
<p>Help is greatly appreciated!  Thanks :-) </p>
